  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:33:19.788Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:11:16.386Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:11:16.372Z",
  "id": 203718655173454,
  "uuid": "6c86fb18-cd5a-4a7c-9826-de0882ce72a2",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "aec920c3-5a84-539c-760b-ba3b8f709d97",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "7b8d0c2d-1e16-eab6-8dd4-09c2d5af6e76",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "We caught up with Kipruto, as he likes to be called, to find out his AKU student experience and future plans as an ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "AKU alumni. ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.aku.edu/alumni/Pages/home.aspx",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_self",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "What's your career story? ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "I have always wanted to be a journalist. While in primary school, I used to imitate radio presenters, so I knew I was destined to be one. I have schooled in public institutions all my life, until I joined AKU. Interestingly, the primary and high schools and even the university I attended were within a 25-kilometre radius of each other. I studied information sciences at Moi University, and I am a blend of IT, publishing, records management and library science (a toxic combination if you ask me). But my major was in media and publishing, I have worked for two media houses, Radio Africa and currently The Standard newspaper where I am an editor. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "How did you know about AKU? ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "I always knew AKU as a medical college, so I was a bit taken back when my boss told me they offer graduate studies in media. That's how I got interested. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Why did you choose to join the MA Digital Journalism programme?  ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "I joined the programme, first because of the digital aspect of the course. Journalism is undergoing a digital shift and I knew the course would help me move with the tide. Secondly, I was extremely impressed with the recruitment process -- it showed from the onset that this was a serious undertaking. I am pleased to say MA DJ has lived up to my expectation, notwithstanding the fact that we are the pioneer cohort.   ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "How was the learning experience?  ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "I have huge respect and admiration for the faculty and I'm going to miss them. Most of them have become good friends -- they were ever willing to help. They (faculty) are like peers really, as they took a hands-on teaching approach. Special mention goes to Dr Rhonda Breit and Stephen Buckley. I would also like to applaud the GSMC staff as they were very helpful. The campus itself is a wonderful place to be, it gave us the ideal environment to learn.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "You were sponsored for a conference in the Karachi campus, tell us more about that.  ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Where do I begin? So much to say about that trip to Pakistan. The student experience conference Parwaaz, as it was called, was such a pleasant experience. I got to meet a lot of people from different backgrounds, and it was so special to learn and share our experiences in the higher education sector; the parallels between the systems in Kenya and the rest of the countries where AKU has a presence. I learnt about this conference through the faculty and it interested me immediately. I loved everything about Karachi, from the people to the food. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "What impact has MA Digital Journalism had on your life or career? ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The course has been hugely beneficial. As a newspaper editor, I no longer think of the stories as just for print but for the website too. I can proudly say that thanks to the course, I can do a story for TV and radio. I learnt how to operate a camera, produce a TV feature and manage the production process. I can proudly say that thanks to MA DJ, I am an all-rounded journalist. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Would you advise anyone to join AKU - specifically the MA Digital Journalism programme? ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Absolutely. You want an international-standard education? Join AKU! ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
